  "enhanced_information": "Virgin T lymphocytes extravasate to lymph nodes primarily using CCR7 and L-selectin. CCR7 is essential for guiding T cells towards the lymph nodes by binding to the chemokine CCL21, while L-selectin facilitates the initial rolling and adhesion of T cells on high endothelial venules (HEVs) in the lymph nodes. This combination is critical for successful extravasation. Other options do not align with the known functions of these molecules in lymphocyte trafficking.",
